# Providers' own windows (decision 090): kept beside the island's state, not in it.
# Only just after the user acted on the provider; several per provider, up to a limit.

scenario: a window opens only just after the user acted on its provider
open-window timer full              -> opened=notnow windows=none     # nothing pops up by itself
acted timer
open-window timer full              -> opened=opened windows=timer/full front=timer/full page=timer/full:a
close-window timer full             -> windows=none
wait 3001
open-window timer full              -> opened=notnow windows=none     # too long after: windowOpenGrace

scenario: the user's action is the provider's own
acted media
open-window timer full              -> opened=notnow windows=none
acted timer
open-window timer full              -> opened=opened

scenario: opening an open window raises it, with its new content, and keeps its page
acted timer
open-window timer full
open-window timer stats             -> windows=timer/full,timer/stats front=timer/stats
pick-page timer full b              -> page=timer/full:b
open-window timer full              -> opened=raised windows=timer/full,timer/stats front=timer/full page=timer/full:b
open-window timer full page=c       -> page=timer/full:c          # asked for a page: that one

scenario: raising needs the user too
acted timer
open-window timer full
open-window timer stats             -> front=timer/stats
wait 5000
open-window timer full              -> opened=notnow front=timer/stats

scenario: new content keeps the user where they are, unless their page went
acted timer
open-window timer full page=b
update-window timer full pages=a,b  -> page=timer/full:b
update-window timer full pages=a,c  -> page=timer/full:a          # its page went: the first
wait 60000
update-window timer full pages=a    -> windows=timer/full         # no user needed: nothing comes forward
update-window timer gone            -> windows=timer/full         # not open: nothing

scenario: a page that doesn't exist isn't picked
acted timer
open-window timer full
pick-page timer full z              -> page=timer/full:a
pick-page timer other a             -> windows=timer/full

scenario: an unknown page asked for opens the first
acted timer
open-window timer full page=z       -> page=timer/full:a

scenario: one id per provider; two providers may use the same id
acted timer
acted notes
open-window timer main
open-window notes main              -> windows=timer/main,notes/main front=notes/main
close-window timer main             -> windows=notes/main

scenario: a provider has at most windowsPerProvider open
acted pad
open-window pad a
open-window pad b
open-window pad c
open-window pad d                   -> opened=opened
open-window pad e                   -> opened=toomany windows=pad/a,pad/b,pad/c,pad/d
open-window pad a                   -> opened=raised              # an open one still comes forward
acted other
open-window other a                 -> opened=opened              # the limit is per provider

scenario: a bad id is refused
acted timer
open-window timer ../../x           -> opened=badid windows=none
open-window timer a/b               -> opened=badid

scenario: a provider stopping takes its windows, and its last action, with it
acted timer
acted notes
open-window timer full
open-window notes main
stop-provider timer                 -> windows=notes/main
open-window timer full              -> opened=notnow              # started again: the user acts first

scenario: windows don't change the island
start timer
acted timer
open-window timer full              -> Compact windows=timer/full expanded=none
click                               -> Expanded expanded=timer
esc                                 -> Compact windows=timer/full # Esc on the island is the island's
